    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Write a practical message",
    "subtitle": "What the speaker means · 1",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to interpret a qualification, reason or contrast and distinguish it from a literal misreading.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U3-27-required-composition-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Compose a purposeful message",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U3-27-required-composition-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "written",
            "prompt": "What the speaker means · 1: Write a practical explanation for someone joining the situation late. State the problem, a supported reason or constraint, and a clear proposed next step.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "我和朋友去图书馆。门口没有人，里面也听不到声音。朋友说：“看来今天没开门，我们回去吧。”我看见门可以打开，想先进去看一看。\n\n进门以后，我们看见很多人坐着看书。他们没有大声说话，所以外面听不见。我说，看起来安静，不是没有人，也不是不能进。\n\n朋友找到一本书，书外面很旧，说这书看上去不怎么样。我打开以后，发现里面有很清楚的地图，写的是我们下个星期要去的地方。\n\n我们坐下看了半个小时。朋友说，在他看来，新书总比旧书好，今天才知道不一定。我说要看自己需要什么，不能只看外面。\n\n走的时候，门口也没有多少人。我们知道图书馆开着，也没有因为书旧就不看。今天两次先看里面，都发现了和第一次想的不一样的事。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Write your own message",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed writing practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "The problem, constraint and next step connect coherently."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I distinguished the source facts from my proposal."
              }
            ],
            "minLength": 1
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
    ],
